# Trivy ignore list for the workspace image (CRITICAL/HIGH, fixed-only gate in CI).
# Every entry: the affected component, why it cannot be fixed here, and when it is
# re-evaluated. Re-evaluate on the next Dependabot bump of the base image or of the tool
# versions in the Dockerfile; drop an entry as soon as an upstream release carries the fix.

# 2026-10-21: usr/local/bin/vault (gobinary), Go crypto/x509. Vault 2.2.0 is the latest
# upstream release and ships with the vulnerable Go standard library; the CLI only talks
# to the company's Vault over TLS it already trusts. Re-evaluate at the next Vault release.
CVE-2026-111943

# 2026-10-28 (#99): usr/local/bin/vault (gobinary), go-jose v4.1.5 (fixed in 4.1.6): a
# DoS when parsing JWKs that contain RSA keys. Vault 2.2.1, the latest release, still
# ships 4.1.5. In the workspace the CLI only reads secrets and logs in to the company's
# Vault over trusted TLS; it does not parse untrusted JWK sets, so the worst case is
# one developer's CLI command failing. Re-evaluate at the next Vault release.
CVE-2026-116587

# 2026-11-11 (#207; owner accepted the risk 2026-11-11): usr/local/bin/vault (gobinary),
# golang.org/x/net v0.60.0 (fixed in 0.62.0): a DoS via crafted HTML input in x/net/html.
# Vault 2.2.1 is the latest release. The workspace CLI only talks to the company's Vault
# over trusted TLS and never parses untrusted HTML. Review by 2026-12-11; drop this entry at
# the first Vault release built with x/net >= 0.62.0.
CVE-2026-78661
